    {
      "id": 50,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        40,
        -520
      ],
      "size": [
        680,
        600
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 50,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## How to make videos\n\n1. Make pictures in the **bigLust** recipe (the other tab). In its\n   Preview & Pick panel, click the picture(s) you want, then click\n   **Send to Video Queue**.\n2. Come to this tab. Your pictures are now in **THE QUEUE** (the 9 boxes on\n   the left).\n3. Click a slot. In the RIGHT prompt box, type what should MOVE - e.g.\n   \"she slowly turns her head and smiles, hair sways, she breathes\".\n   Each slot has its own prompt. Empty = no motion words, the model guesses.\n   The **Copy from previous prompt** button re-uses the last one.\n4. Pick a **size** and **length** with the preset buttons (or leave the\n   defaults).\n5. Press **Run** (top right). If **Auto-start** is ticked, sending images\n   already pressed Run for you. The queue works through the slots one by one.\n6. Each finished video **auto-saves** to `output/freedom_video/`. To also\n   drop a copy in your own folder, use **Set User Save Folder** then\n   **Save to my folder** on STEP 9.\n\nVideo is slow on a 12 GB card - a 5-second clip is a few minutes. That's\nnormal.\n"
      ],
      "title": "READ ME FIRST",
      "color": "#322",
      "bgcolor": "#533"
    },
    {
      "id": 51,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        780,
        -140
      ],
      "size": [
        400,
        230
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 51,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "**Wan 2.2** is the model that turns a still picture into moving video.\n\nYou never change this box. It just loads `Wan2.2-TI2V-5B` (the compressed\n5-billion version - the one that fits your card)."
      ],
      "title": "STEP 1 - the video model",
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    },
    {
      "id": 52,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        780,
        380
      ],
      "size": [
        400,
        340
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 52,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "**A LoRA is a small file that teaches the model ONE thing** - a camera\nmove, a facial expression, a body motion. You stack it on top of Wan here.\n\n**This box is OFF right now** (orange, greyed) because you have no Wan\nmotion LoRAs yet. To turn it on:\n1. Get one (see `comfyui_ext/LORA_SOURCES.md`, the **Video motion LoRAs**\n   section - and mind the Base model: `Wan Video 2.2` works here, an\n   `SDXL`/`Pony` expression LoRA goes on the bigLust IMAGE step instead). Drop the `.safetensors` in the loras folder.\n2. Right-click this box -> **Mode -> Always**.\n3. Choose the file in **lora_name**.\n4. Put the LoRA's **trigger word** into your motion prompt (it's on the\n   download page).\n\n### strength_model  -  the \"how hard it pushes\" dial\nThink volume knob: **left = subtle, right = strong, too far right = broken.**\n- **0.0**  - off, nothing happens.\n- **~0.5** - a gentle hint. Use this if the LoRA melts the face or warps\n  the body.\n- **1.0**  - normal full amount. **Start here.**\n- **1.2 - 1.5** - crank it. Only if the motion is too weak at 1.0. Higher\n  than this almost always distorts the picture.\n- **-1.0** - do the OPPOSITE of what the LoRA learned. Rarely useful.\n\nStacking two LoRAs? Add another **LoraLoaderModelOnly** box after this one\nand keep each strength lower (~0.6 - 0.8) so they don't fight.\n"
      ],
      "title": "STEP 2 - the LoRA add-on  (read this)",
      "color": "#3a2a1a",
      "bgcolor": "#5a4020"
    },
    {
      "id": 53,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        780,
        740
      ],
      "size": [
        360,
        160
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 53,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "**shift** controls how bold the motion is overall.\n- **around 5** = calm, small movements. Use for portraits, talking,\n  breathing.\n- **8** = the default - a good balance.\n- **10 - 12** = big, dramatic motion. Use for action. Too high = jittery\n  or morphing.\n\nLeft = calm, right = wild."
      ],
      "title": "STEP 3 - motion strength (shift)",
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    },
    {
      "id": 54,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1240,
        -110
      ],
      "size": [
        420,
        180
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 54,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "**STEP 4 (green)** fills itself from the queue slot you're working on -\ndon't type here, type in the queue panel's right box.\n\nWrite what MOVES, not what the picture looks like (that's already set by the\npicture). Good: \"she leans forward, lips part, slow breath\". Bad: \"red hair,\nfreckles\" (the picture already has those).\n\n**STEP 5 (red)** is the \"don't do this\" list - mainly \"static / frozen\" so\nyou actually get movement. Leave it alone."
      ],
      "title": "STEP 4-5 - the words",
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    },
    {
      "id": 55,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1680,
        430
      ],
      "size": [
        300,
        250
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 55,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "**steps** - how many passes. **20** is fine for Wan 5B. More (30) =\nslightly smoother, slower. Fewer (12) = faster, rougher.\n\n**cfg** - how hard it obeys your words.\n- **~3.5** = loose, more natural motion, may ignore some of your prompt.\n- **5** = the default - obeys but stays natural.\n- **7+** = obeys hard, can look stiff or over-cooked.\nLeft = free, right = strict.\n\n**sampler / scheduler** - `euler` / `simple` works well for Wan. Leave them.\n\n**control_after_generate**: `randomize` = new motion each Run. `fixed` = keep\nthe same motion while you tweak words."
      ],
      "title": "STEP 7 - make the motion",
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    },
    {
      "id": 56,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        2020,
        740
      ],
      "size": [
        560,
        200
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 56,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "**STEP 9 - save + make it longer**\n\nEvery clip **auto-saves** to `output/freedom_video/` the moment it finishes - you can't lose one.\n\n- **Set User Save Folder** -> pick your own folder (remembered in this workflow). **Save to my folder** -> drops a copy of the last clip there.\n- **Format**: MP4 plays everywhere (default) / WebM is smaller for web / MOV is for video editors.\n\n**Extend video length** -> sends the finished clip back into the queue as a **green slot** (its last frame + its saved prompt come along). Type any extra motion, Run, and the new piece is joined onto the end. Do it as many times as you want.\n\nPicking **10 / 15 / 20 s** does this for you automatically - it makes the clip in ~5-second pieces and joins them. Each piece is a few minutes, so a 20-second clip is a long wait."
      ],
      "title": "STEP 9 - saving",
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    },
    {
      "id": 57,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        40,
        860
      ],
      "size": [
        680,
        150
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 54,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "**Green-framed slots** in the queue came from a video (via Extend, or the **Load a video to extend** button). They carry the video's own saved motion prompt - click one and it shows in the right prompt box, ready to edit. When a green slot runs, the new footage is **joined onto the end** of that video."
      ],
      "title": "green slots = from a video",
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    }
